From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:26:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: apply the source PLL parents again at power-on

The DSI byte and pixel source clocks get the DSI PHY PLLs as parents from
assigned-clock-parents, applied once when the DSI host probes. If the bootloader
powered the PHY down but left the RCG selecting its PLL (the Surface Duo's ABL does
this for DSI0), the switch fails at probe ("rcg didn't update its configuration",
-EBUSY), the clock framework keeps the RCG on the XO and nothing tries again: at
power-on the pixel clock rate cannot be set (-EINVAL) and the panel stays dark.

The PHY PLL runs when msm_dsi_host_power_on() sets the link clock rates, so apply
the defaults again there. It is a no-op when the parents are already right.

Tested on a Surface Duo: booted by ABL both panels now light (DSI0 stayed dark);
booted through UEFI nothing changes.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index c140c922d..a9fbc9d17 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/clk/clk-conf.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/err.h>
@@ -2456,6 +2457,16 @@ int msm_dsi_host_power_on(struct mipi_dsi_host *host,
 	}
 
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(&msm_host->pdev->dev);
+	/*
+	 * The byte/pixel source clocks get their PHY PLL parents from assigned-clock-parents
+	 * at probe. If the PLL was off then (a bootloader that powered the DSI PHY down but
+	 * left the RCG selecting it), the switch fails and the RCG stays on the XO in the
+	 * clock framework. The PHY PLL runs now, so apply the parents again; this is a no-op
+	 * when they are already set.
+	 */
+	ret = of_clk_set_defaults(msm_host->pdev->dev.of_node, false);
+	if (ret)
+		pr_warn("%s: re-applying the source PLL failed: %d\n", __func__, ret);
 	ret = cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_set_rate(msm_host);
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_enable(msm_host);
